5425	You rode the wind from the harbor? This is the Upside-down Forest, grown hanging from the island's underside.
5426	With the wind gone, the forest grew wild and murklings swarm. Clear out twenty for me.
5427	The vine bridge east of Firefly Hollow has snapped. Root Nestkeepers hold tough vines. Four and we can weave it again.
5428	It's Solbaram. Seen the root clods? They're the soil that held up the old trees, but with the wind gone they walk around. Let twelve of them rest.
5429	I'm Knot, the smith here. Sap from this forest gets tougher than iron when it hardens. Find me five lumps. Moss flufflings and thorn pods carry it here, instead of salt flufflings.
5430	The Overturned Elder Tree stands at Old Tree Stump. They say it bursts roots from the ground in rows and drops seeds like hail.
5431	When enraged it shoots thorns in every direction, so watch for the gaps.
5432	People walk the forest paths again. Thank you.
5433	The vine bridge is woven again! Beyond it: Vine Ferry, Root Cliff, and Old Tree Stump.
5434	Thank you. The soil is finding its place again.
5435	Good, that's a year's worth of quenching. Here's your pay.
5436	…The forest is breathing! The upside-down trees sway in the wind.
5437	But there's a rumble at the end of the wind. It's from the Thunder Nest.
